By symmetry, we can focus on the octant where $x,$ $y,$ $z$ are all positive.  In this octant, the condition $|x| + |y| = 1$ becomes $x + y = 1,$ which is the equation of a plane.  Hence, the set of points in this octant such that $|x| + |y| \le 1$ is the set of points bound by the plane $x + y = 1,$ $x = 0,$ and $y = 0.$

